Cross on a text field opens the on-screen keyboard.

The first thing q3rally asks a new player is a profile name, and a player holding only
a pad had no way to type one. The engine starts SDL text input once for the whole
session (`IN_Init`), and the SDL backend opens the system keyboard only when a title
asks for it (`SDL_ENABLE_SCREEN_KEYBOARD`), so that start-up call does not pop a
keyboard over the first frame.

- `sdl/sdl_input.c`: an `in_screenkeyboard` command that sets the hint for one
  `SDL_StartTextInput`, which opens the keyboard. What the player enters arrives as
  SDL_TEXTINPUT, which the engine already delivers to the focused field as characters.
- `q3_ui/ui_mfield.c`: Cross on any text field runs that command. Every field the UI
  draws goes through `MenuField_Key`, so the profile name, the player name and a
  server address all get it.

